{"id": "clm:4f242f53682b7e1084597755107fb47c3b0f326baa485fd0a4fee235de2b2a92", "type": "statement", "text": "In a 2014 randomized trial of 191 people with PD and daily-activity difficulties, a 10-week home occupational-therapy intervention improved self-perceived daily activity performance at 3 months compared with usual care without occupational therapy; the endpoint does not establish disease modification. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24726066/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Living well with PD: driving, work, travel and daily living"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d6b5a9991c7a266016e1f2251838e5010f4435161056c6cb06f5a7f7233d76fb", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:3df8e0d999df6b23f9bebafebea3731d634a1bc70975340dbada0427b7d856ec", "ev:661180dfd3438bd2702234533e05af539721a063b5efcbd83c7ed17d31278b1c", "ev:72189d691978554938d23d1a22430d0c5098524e979eb9ddfb5813de87505262", "ev:a27546b494c7723322ba30bea2fdd86cfe1741b0bc461590bcc11f4f41c78b4e"]}
{"id": "clm:d45aff1cf16b1ffd32680b85bc6f1ae3b0c904ea54b0b06bd32b2bd7a1e42d3e", "type": "statement", "text": "In a Parkinson’s UK forum discussion, one traveler with PD reported that advance wheelchair assistance helped with airport queues and walking; this is an individual experience rather than evidence that one itinerary is best for everyone. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://forum.parkinsons.org.uk/t/long-distance-air-travel-uk-to-australia-advice-please/43760", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Living well with PD: driving, work, travel and daily living"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d6b5a9991c7a266016e1f2251838e5010f4435161056c6cb06f5a7f7233d76fb", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:447ae74f8d4430b3c3a0a80757d67ede94620c99de082ed3f11a586769a3a346"]}
{"id": "clm:f8ee3ae05661a5e8859a08f11262da4fb044c1b32de5f820375af370b9801dba", "type": "statement", "text": "A PD diagnosis alone does not determine whether someone can drive safely; the Parkinson’s Foundation advises assessment of the individual’s symptoms and other age-related changes. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.parkinson.org/living-with-parkinsons/management/activities-daily-living/driving", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Living well with PD: driving, work, travel and daily living"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d6b5a9991c7a266016e1f2251838e5010f4435161056c6cb06f5a7f7233d76fb", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5dac6ef1c335e94164f942a7713f03bec11b1682585284bd27d3a2775b674b3a"]}
{"id": "clm:68a1c630a8ce960dc91bc6c6be473fe70eeb90e691cc4b407d75950d167a47b4", "type": "statement", "text": "Driving fitness assessment should consider motor function, cognition, vision, sleepiness and medication effects; specialist on-road and off-road assessment can help resolve concerns. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10928339/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Living well with PD: driving, work, travel and daily living"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.parkinson.org/living-with-parkinsons/management/activities-daily-living/driving"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d6b5a9991c7a266016e1f2251838e5010f4435161056c6cb06f5a7f7233d76fb", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:aec00bf0bf3a3f751b669e70a37a7514fca94e704d4204e75f933e6d518a8a50", "ev:fce86b4dbaab6ddb197be9ccb0837dd47a2486181bd835e8b931da8e6365241a"]}
{"id": "clm:80f284ed1a2fdfbf178e008a3c75c3894cb6171a1403f416324a113f853ffc4d", "type": "statement", "text": "For time-zone travel, the Parkinson’s Foundation advises preserving the prescribed intervals between doses; Davis Phinney Foundation travel guidance likewise recommends planning a consistent medication schedule. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.parkinson.org/living-with-parkinsons/management/traveling", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Living well with PD: driving, work, travel and daily living"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://davisphinneyfoundation.org/blog/travel-with-greater-ease-parkinsons/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d6b5a9991c7a266016e1f2251838e5010f4435161056c6cb06f5a7f7233d76fb", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:aa0c96d8032d44962496e98cdcf1d64a29bdf9afebe2d44b27af1edd54506023", "ev:b2512ccd96ac66899ff562095d6acf7354d9db97a3b6ef875ef5355db8edee09"]}
{"id": "clm:768bdebc94b87fb4b5126c9cb9a6a6178bf781d95ca60eaa08da734631e955af", "type": "statement", "text": "Travel planning guidance recommends allowing extra time, scheduling rest around arrival, and avoiding an overloaded itinerary. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.parkinson.org/living-with-parkinsons/management/traveling", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Living well with PD: driving, work, travel and daily living"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://davisphinneyfoundation.org/blog/travel-with-greater-ease-parkinsons/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d6b5a9991c7a266016e1f2251838e5010f4435161056c6cb06f5a7f7233d76fb", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:50e68156b9228bd733a5e5c558efc80e9e46256279901a515d15c355b637a94e", "ev:5875d77194344d82ea240ce91f4a2415ddf381e7360265840288ee40d435a0c9", "ev:f91f512225b39f6a551534d089e3eba3e37c5e935d3533bafc410b3f9cb6f5fb"]}
{"id": "clm:18ab9063ba5a94b5f184816534d9bab8316cc20b28c7024551c26a737f0c5df3", "type": "statement", "text": "How long a person continues working after PD diagnosis varies with job demands, symptoms and circumstances; Parkinson’s Europe describes contrasting personal experiences of continuing work and leaving work. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.parkinson.org/library/fact-sheets/employment", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Living well with PD: driving, work, travel and daily living"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://parkinsonseurope.org/parkinsonslife/navigating-the-workplace-with-parkinsons-disease/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d6b5a9991c7a266016e1f2251838e5010f4435161056c6cb06f5a7f7233d76fb", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:87bac94d6f892c428323b4ce04c759696aecbe972d04953733992f4e57643d5f", "ev:ae7c864bea3a679b529eee0b7fecee30638aaddb92e21c766853de32e8e9e93d", "ev:f59e0fa3249370919554123c3400e09ac0ea3727ecbe073201bf96da6c4e1683"]}
